        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0cd864c8-f433-59cd-a05e-1d79452cd84f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nicholas Medforth-Mills, Michael I of Romania\n- Roles: King of Romania, Prince of Romania\n- Places: Romania\n- Concepts: Romanian royal succession, defunct throne, family statute\n\nFacts:\n- Michael I of Romania was born on 25 October 1921.\n- Michael I of Romania reigned as King of Romania from 20 July 1927 to 8 June 1930.\n- Michael I of Romania reigned again as King of Romania from 6 September 1940 until his abdication on 30 December 1947.\n- In 2007, a new family statute placed Nicholas Medforth-Mills, a grandson of Michael I of Romania, third in line to the defunct Romanian throne.\n- The 2007 family statute also conferred the title Prince of Romania on Nicholas Medforth-Mills.\n- In 2015, the title Prince of Romania held by Nicholas Medforth-Mills was abrogated.",
